{
  "requirement": "Interning through any clone makes the handle and its data available through every clone. A fresh cache has its own assignments.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.shared_node_ids`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. Interning through any clone must give a handle that every clone can use.\n2. Interning through any clone must make the data available through every clone.\n3. A fresh cache must have its own assignments, so it doesn't share handles or data with the cache it was not cloned from.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Obligations 1 and 2.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[clones_interning_the_same_data_concurrently_get_one_handle]` creates a cache, hands four clones to separate threads, and has each intern `Node(42)` after a barrier.\n  - It asserts that all returned ids are equal.\n  - It asserts that the original cache's `node_data(ids[0])` returns `Node(42)`. Data interned through the clones is therefore visible through the original.\n  - This would catch a clone that copies the cache's state or keeps a separate map. In that case the original couldn't resolve the id.\n  - It asserts that `Node(43)` gets a different handle, so sharing doesn't collapse distinct data.\n- **Obligation 1, other direction.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[saved_node_and_edge_inputs_survive_a_different_handle_allocation_order]` interns `Node(1)` through the original, via the review setup. It then asserts that `first.clone().cache().intern_node(Node(1)) == subject`. A handle assigned through the original is therefore available through a clone.\n- **Obligation 3.** The same test builds `fresh` with `ValidationCache::new()` and checks two things.\n  - `fresh.cache().node_data(subject)` is `None`, so the fresh cache has no data from the first cache.\n  - `fresh_target` (interned first in the fresh cache) differs from `target` (interned second in the original cache). The fresh cache therefore has its own assignments, and loaded evidence is re-mapped to the fresh handles.\n\n**Minor gap, not treated as a defect**\nNo test reads `node_data` through a clone for data interned through the original. The two tests above show that clones and the original share one assignment table, and that makes this case redundant.\n\nNo acknowledgments or fixmes apply.",
